<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nanbu Nobunao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1546–1599</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nanbu Nobunao was head of the Nanbu warrior family of northern Mutsu in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. In 1590 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> confirmed him in his lands, though he lost the Tsugaru region to his breakaway retainer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsugaru-tamenobu">Tsugaru Tamenobu</a>. He moved his seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morioka">Morioka</a>, where his successors ruled the Morioka domain, known for its horses, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a> until 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nanbu-nobunao.jpg" alt="Nanbu Nobunao" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nanbu_Nobunao.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
